extends layout
//- The account hierarchy. Needs page, view (LandscapeDto), selected (NodeDto).
block actions
  - import neko.platform.presentation.web.icons : icon;
  .btn-list
    a.btn(href="/landscape/assignments")
      | !{icon("apps")}
      | Service assignments
    a.btn(href="/landscape/recovery")
      | !{icon("arrows-exchange")}
      | Disaster recovery
    - if (page.isBillingRead)
      a.btn(href="/landscape/billing")
        | !{icon("chart-line")}
        | Billing
    - if (page.isLandscapeManage)
      button.btn(hx-get="/landscape/directories/new", hx-target="#dialog-host")
        | !{icon("folder")}
        | Directory
      button.btn.btn-primary(hx-get="/landscape/subaccounts/new", hx-target="#dialog-host")
        | !{icon("plus")}
        | Subaccount
block content
  p.text-secondary The global account holds the contract, the purchased entitlements, its administrators and global role collections. Directories group subaccounts and may take over a budget (entitlements) and role collections. Subaccounts are logically separate, each with its own administrators, user group and selected services; each has one or more tenants, and each tenant one or more spaces (always “default”). Every subaccount lives in a region and can fail over to a secondary one (disaster recovery).
  include landscape_body
